4. Ablations:
   - MDGEN trained on full-density data (X_full) as an upper-bound ablative control → if even full-trained MDGEN fails, metric is too strict.
   - Vary subsampling factor K to show monotonic degradation → validates that the metric is sensitive to the actual information loss.
5. Reproducibility / seeds: multiple random seeds for (a) training, (b) generation, (c) subsampling (if stochastic); report mean±SE across seeds; N replicates per condition.
